<h1 class='text-xl'>Player Test</h1>

<div class='mb-6'>
  <h2 class='text-lg'>One sound, two players</h2>
  <p class='my-2 text-base'>Same URL, so the same
    <code>Sound</code>. Play or seek either and the other should match exactly.
    The top player positions with modifiers, the bottom one with helpers.</p>

  <Docs::StereoPlayerModifiers @identifier={{@model.url}} />
  <Docs::StereoPlayer @identifier={{@model.url}} />
</div>

<div class='mb-6'>
  <h2 class='text-lg'>Swapping the identifier</h2>
  <p class='my-2 text-base'>One player, a different sound behind it. Every
    helper and modifier bound to the identifier should follow the selection,
    while the service-wide volume stays put. A seekable file and a live stream
    need different controls, so the transport should change with them. The
    sound you leave keeps playing until you start another.</p>

  <Docs::StereoPlayerChanger @sounds={{@model.swappable}} />
</div>

<div class='mb-6'>
  <h2 class='text-lg'>A sound that cannot play</h2>
  <p class='my-2 text-base'>Play should surface the error, not spin forever.</p>

  <Docs::StereoPlayer @identifier={{@model.unplayable}} />
</div>
